   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thank you, Victor. You're verified.\n\nI checked order Q-7801 from Taqueria Luz. It was promised for 6:15 PM and handed to you at 6:45 PM, so it was 30 minutes late. That qualifies for a credit equal to the delivery fee, which is $2.99.\n\nEarlier tonight, at 7:07 PM, a $2.99 late-delivery credit was already added to your account for this order. Our policy doesn't allow compensating the same problem twice, so I can't add anything more. The credit is in your balance and you can use it on a future order.\n\nIs there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Wait, I did talk to someone earlier, but I thought it was a small credit for the late order. Is that the same $2.99 you're talking about? It was really late though, 30 minutes on a Taqueria Luz order is rough."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Yes, it's the same credit. The $2.99 you got earlier is the late-delivery credit for this order. Your account balance is $2.99, and that's the credit.\n\nI understand a 30-minute delay is frustrating. For an order that's 16 to 44 minutes late, our policy sets the compensation at the delivery fee. That's the $2.99 you already received. I can't add more for this delay.\n\nIf you'd like, I can pass your case to a human specialist. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
